---
export const title = 'Selection and bulk actions';
export const order = 300;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';

import dataSource from '../_data-source.json';
---

<p>
  Set <code>selection</code> to choose how rows are selected: <code>none</code> (the default),
  <code>single</code> or <code>multiple</code>.
</p>
<p>
  With <code>selection="multiple"</code>, each row gets a checkbox and the header a select-all
  checkbox for the page. A selected row is tinted and gets an accent bar on its leading edge. While
  rows are selected, a bar covers the header with the count, a <strong>Clear</strong> action and
  whatever you put in the <code>bulk-actions</code> slot. When every row on the page is selected,
  the bar offers <strong>Select all</strong> for the whole data set. The
  <code>selection-change</code> event then reports <code>allPages: true</code>; in managed mode,
  use that flag to act on every item on the server.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang='html'>
  <div style='width: 100%; height: 28rem;'>
    <wc-table id='table-selection' key-field='_id' selection='multiple' label='People'>
      <wc-button slot='bulk-actions' variant='text' size='sm'>
        <wc-icon slot='icon' name='download'></wc-icon>
        Export
      </wc-button>
      <wc-button slot='bulk-actions' variant='text' size='sm' color='danger'>
        <wc-icon slot='icon' name='delete'></wc-icon>
        Delete
      </wc-button>
      <wc-pagination slot='footer'></wc-pagination>
    </wc-table>
  </div>
  <p class='text-body-medium'>Selection: <code id='selection-output'>[]</code></p>

  <script is:inline define:vars={{ dataSource }}>
    const $table = document.getElementById('table-selection');
    $table.columns = [
      { name: 'name', label: 'Name', width: 14 },
      { name: 'company', label: 'Company', width: 12 },
      { name: 'email', label: 'Email', width: 22 },
    ];
    $table.data = dataSource;
    // Inactive people cannot be selected.
    $table.isRowSelectable = row => row.isActive !== false;
    $table.addEventListener('selection-change', event => {
      const { value, allPages } = event.detail;
      document.getElementById('selection-output').textContent = allPages
        ? `all ${value.length} items`
        : JSON.stringify(value);
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Single selection</h3>
<p>
  With <code>selection="single"</code>, each row gets a radio button and selecting a row clears the
  others. Rows carry <code>aria-selected</code>; there is no select-all and no selection bar.
  <kbd>Space</kbd> selects the focused row.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang='html'>
  <div style='width: 100%; height: 20rem;'>
    <wc-table id='table-single' key-field='_id' selection='single' label='People'></wc-table>
  </div>

  <script is:inline define:vars={{ dataSource }}>
    const $single = document.getElementById('table-single');
    $single.columns = [
      { name: 'name', label: 'Name', width: 14 },
      { name: 'company', label: 'Company', width: 12, flex: 1 },
    ];
    $single.data = dataSource.slice(0, 5);
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Rows that cannot be selected</h3>
<p>
  Set the <code>isRowSelectable</code> property to a function of the row. Rows it returns
  <code>false</code> for show a disabled control, carry <code>aria-disabled</code> and are skipped by
  select-all and by <strong>Select all</strong>.
</p>

<h3>Row keys</h3>
<p>
  <code>key-field</code> (default <code>id</code>) names the field that identifies a row. Keys are
  always compared and reported as strings, so a numeric <code>id</code> of <code>1</code> matches
  <code>selected-row-keys='["1"]'</code>, and <code>selection-change</code> reports
  <code>["1"]</code>.
</p>
